            "review_title": "Review at Cork & Fork - Wine and Kitchen",
            "review_text": "Sonal\n7 contributions\n0\nwine & crepes- yummmm\nNov 2018 • Friends\nYesterday, happen to scroll my Facebook page and trying to find a new place to go and hang out with a friend... everything that I could see was same old option. Then while scrolling, found this unique ad” free flow- make your own rules”.\nDefinitely the marketing tactic was unique and it caught attention.\nI invited a friend for evening drinks and we set to meet at the place...expectation was that it will be this new bar same as others in district 1. \nBut while driving through the taxi driver took to the narrow lanes with traffic and it was not usual district 1 for me. I immediately started regretting my choice because I thought how can there be a bar in such conjusted( non conventional) place.\nBut couldn’t have returned back, so reached there and ordered wine and buckwheat crepe.\nAt first interaction with the owner, whole perception changed.\nStaff and owner were really humble, jovial, wine was good at the price we had, crepe was delicious.\nHospitality amazing!\nI am sure it’s a good handout place to have casual drinks with friends or have a small get together.\nAmazing experience!\nRead more\nWritten November 10, 2018",
