            "review_text": "hung_up_the_backpack\nZurich, Switzerland10 contributions\n0\nDelicious crepes, wine and charcuterie\nJul 2018 • Couples\nThe good reviews here and on Google weren't wrong, this small place does excellent crepes, international wines and charcuterie plates (amongst other things). My wife had a mango and nutella crepe with cinnamon and could have eaten five of them it was so good! I had a charcuterie plate with two types of ham, sliced dried sausage and paté (all from France) served with lettuce and warm slices of baguette. The owner recommended a suitable wine based on our preferences, so we ended up having the house white, which was French and dry. I also had a beer from the Pasteur St craft brewery. There were so many crepe options, including matcha, vanilla or chocolate base, and the owner prepared them to order at the front of the shop. Perfect if you want a little taste of what France does best in the middle of hectic downtown HCMC.\nRead more\nWritten July 21, 2018",
